\newlabel{tab:rmse}{{1}{6}{Bernoulli(.5) GATE RMSE (one MCSE in parentheses). Column labels specify estimator and true mechanism. Synthetic entries summarize three fixed graph seeds with 300 experiments each; each public entry has 300. All displayed fits are available. These are different response settings, not a single ranking task}{table.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Two different failure modes. (a) Add under threshold interference: absolute mean conditional endpoint contrast bias versus mean in-assignment signal residual RMSE, for eight graph classes and two designs. Selected labels identify examples; vertical bars use MCSE of the conditional bias, not outcome residuals. (b) Add under correctly specified linear means, Bernoulli assignment: iid residual intervals versus known-covariance intervals. Correlated errors have unit marginal variance throughout. Coverage bars are Wilson 95\% intervals across assignments/noise; the dotted line is .95.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:failure}{{2}{6}{Two different failure modes. (a) Add under threshold interference: absolute mean conditional endpoint contrast bias versus mean in-assignment signal residual RMSE, for eight graph classes and two designs. Selected labels identify examples; vertical bars use MCSE of the conditional bias, not outcome residuals. (b) Add under correctly specified linear means, Bernoulli assignment: iid residual intervals versus known-covariance intervals. Correlated errors have unit marginal variance throughout. Coverage bars are Wilson 95\% intervals across assignments/noise; the dotted line is .95}{figure.2}{}}
